<title>USA: US bank measure to be in spending bill - Sen. Lott.</title>
<headline>US bank measure to be in spending bill - Sen. Lott.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Senate Majority Leader Trent Lott said Tuesday measures to bolster the thrift deposit insurance fund and ease regulatory burdens on banks would be included in a broad spending bill.</p>
<p>The provision to bolster the Savings Association Insurance Fund (SAIF) will be included in the spending measure &quot;as a major offset,&quot; Lott told reporters. &quot;We also hope to have some limited bank regulation, deregulation provisions included,&quot; the Republican from Mississippi added.</p>
<p>&quot;There's some things that need to be done with regard to burdens on banks and it's a limited bill, it's not a major deregulation bill,&quot; Lott said.</p>
<p>Senate Minority Leader Tom Daschle, a Democrat from South Dakota, said about the SAIF legislation: &quot;The initial report is favorable and we can be supportive.&quot;</p>
</text>
